<p><b>Submissions</b>:
We accept any kind of submissions for presentation at our workshop: Submissions that are accepted at LoG, submissions accepted elsewhere, submissions that are currently under review at other venues, work in progress, etc. 
</p>

<p>If necessary, we will select submissions based on relevance to the graph learning community.</p>

<p>Authors whose papers/posters are accepted to the workshop will have the opportunity to participate in a pitch and poster session, and several will also be chosen for oral presentation.
The accepted papers/posters will be published on this website and will not be considered archival for resubmission purposes.</p>


<h2 id="keynotes">Keynotes</h2>


<p class="center">

  <img src="https://frareba.github.io/bild.png" width="150px" height="auto"><br/>
  <a href="https://frareba.github.io/" target=_blank>Franka Bause</a><br />
  CISPA Helmholtz Center for Information Security
  </p>

  <p>Franka is a Postdoc in the Relational Machine Learning Lab of Rebekka Burkholz at CISPA Helmholtz Center for Information Security. She completed my doctorate with distinction in the Data Mining and Machine Learning (Machine Learning with Graphs) group at University of Vienna in 2025.
  Both her Bachelor’s and Master’s degrees are from TU Dortmund University, where she graduated with honors in 2020. Frankas research mostly centers around graph learning and similarity measures for graphs, with the aim of improving both efficiency and accuracy.</p>


<p class="center">
  <img src="alice.jpeg" width="150px" height="auto"><br/>
  Alice Moallemy-Oureh<br />
  GASCADE
  </p>

  <p>Alice is in the final phase of her doctoral studies at the University of Kassel. Alongside her research, she works as a Solutions Architect for AI and Innovation at GASCADE. Her doctoral project, GAIN (Graphs in Artificial Intelligence and Neuronal Networks), is carried out in cooperation with Fraunhofer IEE and the University of Kassel. In it, she develops graph neural networks capable of processing attribute-dynamic graphs in continuous time.

  In her role at GASCADE, Alice serves as a central point of contact between different departments. She creates AI solutions and automations that not only drive innovation forward but also make her colleagues’ everyday work easier and more rewarding.
  </p>



